cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SARcasmScope in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "SARcasmScope: A Calibrated Feature-Fusion Framework for Context-Aware Sarcasm Detection in Multilingual and Code-Mixed Text"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
authors:
  - family-names: "Mehta"
    given-names: "Payal"
    email: "payal.12620246@vit.edu"
    affiliation: "Vellore Institute of Technology"
keywords:
  - "sarcasm-detection"
  - "computational-linguistics"
  - "multilingual-nlp"
  - "indic-languages"
  - "hinglish"
  - "marathi"
  - "telugu"
  - "code-mixing"
  - "calibrated-feature-fusion"
  - "selective-prediction"
  - "affective-computing"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/moonlitpayal/sarcasmscope"
abstract: >-
  SARcasmScope is an anti-fragile, calibrated feature-fusion framework that synergizes
  client-side linguistic incongruity analysis, Indic morphological normalization,
  Romanized phonetic folding, and regularized subword semantic representations.
  Evaluated across 5,600 independently partitioned records from 5 established public
  corpora, SARcasmScope improves independent sarcasm recall from 1.37% to 55.93%
  (56.57% Macro-F1) on a frozen held-out test split (N = 1,123), with an inference latency
  under 0.26 ms on standard CPU hardware.
